{
  "info": {
    "name": "NORTHSTAR weekly checkout and orders",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "Local contract checks. Use test accounts and fixture data. Requests create orders and change inventory; never run against production data. Buy now accepts optional buyNow: {productId, variantId: null or ID, quantity: 1..9} in POST /orders/preview and POST /orders. It validates server prices/stock, preserves the cart, and binds the selection to requestId for idempotency. Cart quantities allow nine units per option including existing units. POST /orders/:id/return/cancel accepts {} for the owning customer. Requested or accepted returns become cancelled; cancelled retries are read-only. Completed/rejected/missing requests return 409. Delivery, stock, payments and refunds do not change. Eligible paid Razorpay order cancellation credits the full paid order total to Northstar Wallet atomically with cancellation and stock restoration. refund.method=wallet, refund.status=completed, paymentStatus=refunded. Retries never duplicate credit; no gateway refund is initiated. Unpaid online orders do not receive wallet credit. Existing in-flight gateway refunds cannot be converted. New completed paid returns create a pending wallet refund. Admin POST /admin/orders/:id/refund {destination:\"wallet\"} credits the balance and unique refund ledger atomically. Eligible pending legacy cash refunds may also use this action. Completed cash/gateway refunds and gateway processing cannot be credited again. Replacement: POST /orders/:id/return accepts resolution=refund (default) or replacement. Replacement is for the same products/options/quantities on paid delivered orders. Admin review uses existing return endpoints. Receipt /return/complete transactionally reserves sellable replacement stock without restocking returned units or creating refunds. Admin POST /orders/:id/return/replacement {status} advances ready_to_ship -> shipped -> out_for_delivery -> delivered, with idempotent retries. Customers may cancel requested/accepted replacements and reserved replacements before dispatch; reserved cancellation releases stock and credits the paid amount to the wallet. Replacement progress is returned in returnRequest.replacementStatus. Follow-up requests: after replacement delivery (or unreserved cancellation/rejection), POST /orders/:id/return includes requestCycle=current+1. Earlier requests are archived in returnHistory; references are cycle-specific. All return/replacement mutations accept requestCycle (legacy default 1) and reject stale cycles. A ready-to-ship replacement may be cancelled before dispatch, releasing reserved replacement stock and refunding the paid amount to the wallet exactly once. After dispatch, wait for delivery before requesting another return or replacement."
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:5000/api"
    },
    {
      "key": "customerCookie",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "adminCookie",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "addressId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "productId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "requestId",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Orders require authentication",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/orders"
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"HTTP 401\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Review checkout",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Cookie",
            "value": "{{customerCookie}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/orders/preview",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\"addressId\":\"{{addressId}}\"}"
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"HTTP 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test(\"Server total\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.totalAmount).to.eql(15000));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Place COD order",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Cookie",
            "value": "{{customerCookie}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/orders",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\"addressId\":\"{{addressId}}\",\"paymentMethod\":\"cod\",\"requestId\":\"{{requestId}}\",\"expectedTotalPaise\":15000}"
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"HTTP 201\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"orderId\", pm.response.json().data.order.id);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
